AB  - Accurate breast cancer diagnosis is critical for early intervention and improved patient outcomes. However, the precision of delineating tumor regions and assessing disease severity heavily depends on the clinical expertise of doctors. Recent research efforts in breast ultrasound image segmentation and classification have aimed to support physicians in making faster and more accurate decisions. Nevertheless, many of these studies often sacrifice scalability by relying on large models with numerous parameters and high computational costs. In this paper, we propose a lightweight model named Dual Attention Lightweight U-Net and Visual Geometry Group, designed to perform both segmentation and classification tasks on breast ultrasound images. The proposed model is developed based on the widely adopted Visual Geometry Group and U-Net architectures, integrating depthwise separable convolutional layers and two attention mechanisms, including Attention Gate and Spatial Attention. This design leverages the segmentation results from the U-Net attention mechanism to improve classification accuracy while reducing model complexity. Experimental results on the public Dataset of Breast Ultrasound Images demonstrate that the proposed model achieves an accuracy of 82.69% while using only half the parameters compared to state-of-the-art models, highlighting its potential for scalable and efficient clinical deployment.
