AB  - Accurate traffic flow prediction is a key technology in intelligent transportation systems, crucial for planning future mobility, improving urban traffic efficiency, and supporting decision-making in traffic management. Current mainstream graph convolutional networks typically rely on prior knowledge, using predefined adjacency matrices to model the spatial dependencies within road networks. However, the static representation of spatial correlations using predefined or adaptive adjacency matrices fails to capture the dynamic changes in spatial relationships between road segments over time, thereby limiting the accuracy of traffic flow predictions. To address this issue, we propose the Dynamic Graph Convolutional Recurrent Network with Attention Mechanism for traffic flow forecasting. This method combines dynamic graph convolutional recurrent networks with a dynamic graph generation model based on recurrent neural networks, constructing dynamic graphs through time-varying traffic signals to simultaneously capture both spatial and temporal features. Additionally, the proposed model separates anomalous signals from normal traffic signals and employs a data-driven approach to model the anomalous signals, further improving prediction performance. Finally, we integrate a spatiotemporal attention module to effectively capture long-range, multifaceted spatiotemporal patterns. The realization of this model is based on artificial intelligence technology. Experimental results on four real datasets show that the model proposed in this paper significantly outperforms the current state-of-the-art prediction methods in terms of prediction performance.
