AB  - In this paper, we propose an Advanced Driver Assistance Systems (ADAS) framework that utilizes Signal Temporal Logic (STL) to formally represent driving tasks based on environmental information. A neural network architecture, the STL generator network, is designed to generate tasks that enhance interpretability and guide either driver actions or autonomous control inputs. By integrating coarse task determination and parameter specification networks, the system provides structured task recommendations to improve safety and skill development. The proposed method’s effectiveness is validated through hardware-in-the-loop simulations, demonstrating its potential to enhance driver performance and system transparency in complex driving environments.
